event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":2625,"item_id":"fc_096d8e18fe7ae64d016adb1fc6a4548191aac0e1601a96c926","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"spec\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"wave-map-energy\\\",\\\"full_target\\\":\\\"Let n,m be positive integers. Let u:R^n times (0,infinity) -> R^m be jointly smooth, and let q in R^m have Euclidean norm one. Assume: |u(x,r)|=1; for every (x,r), u_tt-Delta_x u=a u for some real a; and on every compact time interval J contained in (0,infinity), u=q outside a compact set C_J uniformly in r. Define e(x,r)=|u_t(x,r)|^2+sum_{j=1}^n|partial_(x_j)u(x,r)|^2 and E(r)=integral over R^n of e(x,r) dx, Lebesgue measure. Prove e(.,r) is Lebesgue integrable for every r>0, E is differentiable at every r>0, and E'(r)=0.\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"For every r>0, e(.,r) is Lebesgue integrable, E is differentiable at r, and E'(r)=0.\\\",\\\"parameters\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"n\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"m\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"u\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"jointly smooth map R^n×(0,∞)→R^m\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"q\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"unit vector in R^m\\\"}],\\\"hypotheses\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n and r>0, |u(x,r)|=1.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:7-10\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n,r>0 there exists a∈R such that u_tt(x,r)-Δ_xu(x,r)=a u(x,r), with componentwise Δ_x.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:11-13\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H003\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For each compact interval J⊂(0,∞), there is compact C_J⊂R^n such that u(x,r)=q for x∉C_J and r∈J.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:14-16\\\"}],\\\"definitions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"D001\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"e\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"R^n×(0,∞)→R\\\",\\\"definition\\\":\\\"e(x,r)=|u_t(x,r)|²+Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j}u(x,r)|²\\\",\\\"depends_on\\\":[],\\\"requires\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"x\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"R^n\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"(0,∞)\\\"}],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"n\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"D002\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"E\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"(0,∞)→R\\\",\\\"definition\\\":\\\"E(r)=Lebesgue integral over R^n of e(x,r)\\\",\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"D001\\\"],\\\"requires\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"(0,∞)\\\"}],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"D003\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"Δ_x\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"operator on smooth R^m-valued maps\\\",\\\"definition\\\":\\\"Δ_xu=Σ_{j=1}^n∂²_{x_j}u, componentwise\\\",\\\"depends_on\\\":[],\\\"requires\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"n\\\"]}],\\\"logic\\\":{\\\"classical\\\":true,\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"modus_ponens\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\",\\\"implication_introduction\\\",\\\"exists_elimination\\\",\\\"contradiction_classical\\\"],\\\"calculations\\\":[\\\"Finite Euclidean inner-product and finite-sum identities, differentiation of smooth functions and the definition of derivatives. Compactness, uniform continuity, elementary one-variable integration, and iterated integration are established explicitly in the inference arguments; they are not trusted calculation rules.\\\"],\\\"primitives\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"R\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"real numbers\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"Real field, usual topology, and Lebesgue measure.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"R^k\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Euclidean space\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"k-dimensional real Euclidean space with Euclidean inner product and Lebesgue measure.\\\"}]},\\\"pins\\\":{\\\"lean_version\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_root\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},\\\"inputs\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"problem.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"proof-draft.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"source-context.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"}]},\\\"graph\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"wave-map-energy\\\",\\\"spec_sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"propositions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n and r>0, |u(x,r)|=1.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n,r>0 there exists a∈R such that u_tt(x,r)-Δ_xu(x,r)=a u(x,r), with componentwise Δ_x.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"Δ_x\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H003\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For each compact interval J⊂(0,∞), there is compact C_J⊂R^n such that u(x,r)=q for x∉C_J and r∈J.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"q\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"target\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For every r>0, e(.,r) is Lebesgue integrable, E is differentiable at r, and E'(r)=0.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D001\\\",\\\"D002\\\",\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e\\\",\\\"E\\\",\\\"u\\\"]}],\\\"inferences\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D001\\\",\\\"D002\\\",\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r0\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive real number\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S010\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r0>0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"J\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"closed interval contained in (0,∞) with r0 in its interior\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S010\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"witness\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"After proving existence of such an interval, choose J about r0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[\\\"F001\\\"],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r0\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"C_J\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"compact subset of R^n\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S010\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"witness\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Choose the compact set furnished by H003 for J.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"from_local\\\":[\\\"J\\\"],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"J\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"B\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"closed box in R^n containing C_J\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S010\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"witness\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"After establishing existence of a containing box, choose such a box B.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[\\\"F002\\\"],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"C_J\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"j\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"integer with 1≤j≤n\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S007\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S008\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix an arbitrary coordinate index j.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"n\\\"]}],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r0>0. Choose δ>0 smaller than r0 and set J=[r0-δ,r0+δ]; this proves F001: such a compact interval exists and r0 is interior. Choose B as below only after its existence is established. H003 applied to J gives a compact C_J with u=q on its spatial complement. Since C_J is compact it is bounded, so some finite closed coordinate box contains it; this proves F002. Choose J using F001, then C_J by H003 and B using F002. For x outside C_J, u is constant in x and in time throughout the interior of J; differentiability gives u_t=0 and every spatial first derivative zero there. On the boundary the same derivatives vanish by continuity, taking a sequence from the open complement. Thus for r∈J all derivatives, and hence e, vanish off C_J. The function e(.,r) is continuous, bounded on compact C_J and zero off it, so is Lebesgue integrable. Also e(x,s) is smooth in (x,s). On B×J its time derivative e_t is continuous and uniformly continuous. For h≠0 sufficiently small with r0+h∈J, the one-variable fundamental theorem of calculus gives [e(x,r0+h)-e(x,r0)]/h=∫_0^1 e_t(x,r0+θh)dθ. Uniform continuity implies uniform convergence in x∈B of this quotient to e_t(x,r0). Since B has finite measure, the absolute difference between integrals is bounded by measure(B) times the uniform error. As E(s)=∫_B e(x,s)dx for s∈J (e vanishes outside C_J⊂B), this proves differentiability and E'(r0)=∫_B e_t(x,r0)dx. Differentiating the finite sum defining e yields e_t=2u_t·u_tt+2Σ_j u_j·∂_j u_t, where u_j=∂_j u. For each fixed j, f(x)=u_t(x,r0)·u_j(x,r0) is smooth and compactly supported in C_J; ∂_j f=(∂_j u_t)·u_j+u_t·u_jj. Its integral is zero: choose a coordinate interval containing C_J in its interior; for each fixed choice of the other coordinates, f is zero at both endpoints, and the one-variable fundamental theorem gives integral of ∂_j f equal to zero. The derivative is continuous and compactly supported, hence absolutely integrable; integration first in coordinate j and then in the remaining coordinates is valid by Fubini for an absolutely integrable function. Consequently ∫(∂_j u_t)·u_j=−∫u_t·u_jj. Summing over j gives E'(r0)=2∫_{R^n}u_t·(u_tt−Δ_xu)dx. Differentiating |u|²=1 in time gives u·u_t=0. By H002, at each x there is a scalar a with u_tt−Δ_xu=a u; thus u_t·(u_tt−Δ_xu)=a(u_t·u)=0 pointwise. The integrand is zero and E'(r0)=0. As r0 was arbitrary, the asserted result holds at every positive time; no endpoint is used.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r0\\\",\\\"J\\\",\\\"C_J\\\",\\\"B\\\",\\\"j\\\",\\\"e\\\",\\\"E\\\",\\\"u\\\",\\\"q\\\",\\\"n\\\",\\\"u_t\\\",\\\"u_j\\\",\\\"u_tt\\\",\\\"u_jj\\\",\\\"Δ_x\\\",\\\"a\\\",\\\"δ\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"F001\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"There exists a compact interval J⊂(0,∞) having r0 in its interior.\\\",\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r0\\\"],\\\"assumptions\\\":[]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"F002\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"There exists a closed bounded coordinate box B⊂R^n containing C_J.\\\",\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"C_J\\\",\\\"n\\\"],\\\"assumptions\\\":[]}],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[]}]}}\"}"}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":2626,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_096d8e18fe7ae64d016adb1fc6a4548191aac0e1601a96c926","call_id":"call_71d1d831a28a48169c150c53b1fe61d3","name":"submit_artifact","arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"spec\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"wave-map-energy\\\",\\\"full_target\\\":\\\"Let n,m be positive integers. Let u:R^n times (0,infinity) -> R^m be jointly smooth, and let q in R^m have Euclidean norm one. Assume: |u(x,r)|=1; for every (x,r), u_tt-Delta_x u=a u for some real a; and on every compact time interval J contained in (0,infinity), u=q outside a compact set C_J uniformly in r. Define e(x,r)=|u_t(x,r)|^2+sum_{j=1}^n|partial_(x_j)u(x,r)|^2 and E(r)=integral over R^n of e(x,r) dx, Lebesgue measure. Prove e(.,r) is Lebesgue integrable for every r>0, E is differentiable at every r>0, and E'(r)=0.\\\",\\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"For every r>0, e(.,r) is Lebesgue integrable, E is differentiable at r, and E'(r)=0.\\\",\\\"parameters\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"n\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"m\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive integer\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"u\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"jointly smooth map R^n×(0,∞)→R^m\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"q\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"unit vector in R^m\\\"}],\\\"hypotheses\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n and r>0, |u(x,r)|=1.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:7-10\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n,r>0 there exists a∈R such that u_tt(x,r)-Δ_xu(x,r)=a u(x,r), with componentwise Δ_x.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:11-13\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H003\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For each compact interval J⊂(0,∞), there is compact C_J⊂R^n such that u(x,r)=q for x∉C_J and r∈J.\\\",\\\"origin\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md:14-16\\\"}],\\\"definitions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"D001\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"e\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"R^n×(0,∞)→R\\\",\\\"definition\\\":\\\"e(x,r)=|u_t(x,r)|²+Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j}u(x,r)|²\\\",\\\"depends_on\\\":[],\\\"requires\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"x\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"R^n\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"(0,∞)\\\"}],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"n\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"D002\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"E\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"(0,∞)→R\\\",\\\"definition\\\":\\\"E(r)=Lebesgue integral over R^n of e(x,r)\\\",\\\"depends_on\\\":[\\\"D001\\\"],\\\"requires\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"(0,∞)\\\"}],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"D003\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"Δ_x\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"operator on smooth R^m-valued maps\\\",\\\"definition\\\":\\\"Δ_xu=Σ_{j=1}^n∂²_{x_j}u, componentwise\\\",\\\"depends_on\\\":[],\\\"requires\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"n\\\"]}],\\\"logic\\\":{\\\"classical\\\":true,\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"modus_ponens\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\",\\\"implication_introduction\\\",\\\"exists_elimination\\\",\\\"contradiction_classical\\\"],\\\"calculations\\\":[\\\"Finite Euclidean inner-product and finite-sum identities, differentiation of smooth functions and the definition of derivatives. Compactness, uniform continuity, elementary one-variable integration, and iterated integration are established explicitly in the inference arguments; they are not trusted calculation rules.\\\"],\\\"primitives\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"R\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"real numbers\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"Real field, usual topology, and Lebesgue measure.\\\"},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"R^k\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"Euclidean space\\\",\\\"meaning\\\":\\\"k-dimensional real Euclidean space with Euclidean inner product and Lebesgue measure.\\\"}]},\\\"pins\\\":{\\\"lean_version\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_commit\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"mathlib_root\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\"},\\\"inputs\\\":[{\\\"path\\\":\\\"frozen-target.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"problem.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"proof-draft.json\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"},{\\\"path\\\":\\\"source-context.md\\\",\\\"sha256\\\":\\\"placeholder\\\"}]},\\\"graph\\\":{\\\"format_version\\\":2,\\\"case_id\\\":\\\"wave-map-energy\\\",\\\"spec_sha256\\\":\\\"controller-bound\\\",\\\"propositions\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n and r>0, |u(x,r)|=1.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H002\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For all x∈R^n,r>0 there exists a∈R such that u_tt(x,r)-Δ_xu(x,r)=a u(x,r), with componentwise Δ_x.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"Δ_x\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"H003\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For each compact interval J⊂(0,∞), there is compact C_J⊂R^n such that u(x,r)=q for x∉C_J and r∈J.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"q\\\"]},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"target\\\",\\\"statement\\\":\\\"For every r>0, e(.,r) is Lebesgue integrable, E is differentiable at r, and E'(r)=0.\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D001\\\",\\\"D002\\\",\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"binders\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"e\\\",\\\"E\\\",\\\"u\\\"]}],\\\"inferences\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"P\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D001\\\",\\\"D002\\\",\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r0\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive real number\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S010\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r0>0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"J\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"closed interval contained in (0,∞) with r0 in its interior\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S010\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"witness\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"After proving existence of such an interval, choose J about r0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[\\\"F001\\\"],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r0\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"C_J\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"compact subset of R^n\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S002\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S010\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"witness\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Choose the compact set furnished by H003 for J.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"from_local\\\":[\\\"J\\\"],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"J\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"B\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"closed box in R^n containing C_J\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S003\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S010\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"witness\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"After establishing existence of a containing box, choose such a box B.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[\\\"F002\\\"],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"C_J\\\"]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"j\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"integer with 1≤j≤n\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S007\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S008\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix an arbitrary coordinate index j.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"n\\\"]}],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r0>0. Choose δ>0 smaller than r0 and set J=[r0-δ,r0+δ]; this proves F001: such a compact interval exists and r0 is interior. Choose B as below only after its existence is established. H003 applied to J gives a compact C_J with u=q on its spatial complement. Since C_J is compact it is bounded, so some finite closed coordinate box contains it; this proves F002. Choose J using F001, then C_J by H003 and B using F002. For x outside C_J, u is constant in x and in time throughout the interior of J; differentiability gives u_t=0 and every spatial first derivative zero there. On the boundary the same derivatives vanish by continuity, taking a sequence from the open complement. Thus for r∈J all derivatives, and hence e, vanish off C_J. The function e(.,r) is continuous, bounded on compact C_J and zero off it, so is Lebesgue integrable. Also e(x,s) is smooth in (x,s). On B×J its time derivative e_t is continuous and uniformly continuous. For h≠0 sufficiently small with r0+h∈J, the one-variable fundamental theorem of calculus gives [e(x,r0+h)-e(x,r0)]/h=∫_0^1 e_t(x,r0+θh)dθ. Uniform continuity implies uniform convergence in x∈B of this quotient to e_t(x,r0). Since B has finite measure, the absolute difference between integrals is bounded by measure(B) times the uniform error. As E(s)=∫_B e(x,s)dx for s∈J (e vanishes outside C_J⊂B), this proves differentiability and E'(r0)=∫_B e_t(x,r0)dx. Differentiating the finite sum defining e yields e_t=2u_t·u_tt+2Σ_j u_j·∂_j u_t, where u_j=∂_j u. For each fixed j, f(x)=u_t(x,r0)·u_j(x,r0) is smooth and compactly supported in C_J; ∂_j f=(∂_j u_t)·u_j+u_t·u_jj. Its integral is zero: choose a coordinate interval containing C_J in its interior; for each fixed choice of the other coordinates, f is zero at both endpoints, and the one-variable fundamental theorem gives integral of ∂_j f equal to zero. The derivative is continuous and compactly supported, hence absolutely integrable; integration first in coordinate j and then in the remaining coordinates is valid by Fubini for an absolutely integrable function. Consequently ∫(∂_j u_t)·u_j=−∫u_t·u_jj. Summing over j gives E'(r0)=2∫_{R^n}u_t·(u_tt−Δ_xu)dx. Differentiating |u|²=1 in time gives u·u_t=0. By H002, at each x there is a scalar a with u_tt−Δ_xu=a u; thus u_t·(u_tt−Δ_xu)=a(u_t·u)=0 pointwise. The integrand is zero and E'(r0)=0. As r0 was arbitrary, the asserted result holds at every positive time; no endpoint is used.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\",\\\"H003\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r0\\\",\\\"J\\\",\\\"C_J\\\",\\\"B\\